WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:12.870
Good morning everybody, and welcome to this
meeting this morning in London, this meeting

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.990
in public of the Board of NHS England.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:20.300
I would like to extend a special welcome to
those who have joined us in the audience this

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.300
morning.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.760
It is very good that people take such an interest
in our work; and of course, also those who

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.480
are joining us on the live stream.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:35.160
We have a heavy agenda today, and we will
be taking the Board through it in a moment,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.190
but just let me stress once again that the
business of the Board is conducted both in

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:46.460
these formal meetings – one half of which
is in this public arena; it is not a public

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.550
meeting as such, but a meeting of the Board
in public because of our clear and strong

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.150
commitment to the principles of openness and
transparency.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:59.420
Nowhere will that be demonstrated than by
the weight of the decisions that we are being

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.800
required to take this morning.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.689
The other part of our business will be at
the end of this meeting, when we will resolve

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:11.280
to go into a closed session to deal with material
that can only be considered in that way.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.490
I should also stress, of course, though, that
Board members are constantly engaged in the

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:20.439
business of the Board; it is not just when
we appear on your screens or in this room

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:29.420
this morning that we are intellectually and
strategically engaged in the work of the board.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:40.520
Let me then declare the meeting formally open.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:52.740
Secondly, to ask whether there are any declarations
of interest from members of the Board in any

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.340
of the matters on the agenda, other than those
already recorded in the public register?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:04.560
No, thank you.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:11.510
The minutes of the last meeting have been
circulated; may I take those as a fair and

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.480
accurate record of the last meeting?

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.880
Thank you very much.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:21.070
I think we could move on quite quickly then
into the formal business of the meeting, and

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:25.340
I will ask the Chief Executive to speak to
his report.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:31.110
Shall I just say before he does so that, because
of the fast movement of events since the Spending

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:38.220
Review, there has been a need to produce a
number of our papers much later in the cycle

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:44.410
than we would have ordinarily wished to do,
and it will be evident, I think, why that

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.890
will be so when we come to talk about the
allocations paper.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:48.890
On that background.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.330
and with that in mind, may I invite you, Simon,
to talk to your paper.

